  "opal": {
    "why": "The file imports @vitest/expect and @vitest/utils, Vitest's own expect, and tests that implementation's behavior and messages. Loading @vitest/expect defines the global matcher registry, Symbol.for('$$jest-matchers-object'), which opal's expect (Jest's, which defines it the same way) already holds. So the file fails to load with 'Cannot redefine property', and none of its 122 tests run. Jest fails the same way on a file that imports @vitest/expect.",
